# Persian-first RTL

Persian (`fa-IR`) and RTL are mandatory for this doctor–patient platform. Apply them to public physician pages and to administrative, clinical, and financial interfaces.

## Language and direction

- Default language is **Persian (Farsi)** for Iranian users.
- Root HTML must use `lang="fa-IR"` and `dir="rtl"` (and keep them consistent on layout shells).
- Design **RTL from the start** for public physician pages, service management, appointment flows, patient forms, clinical records, prescriptions, financial displays, dialogs, menus, navigation, tables, pagination, and notifications.
- Prefer **CSS logical properties** (`margin-inline`, `padding-inline`, `inset-inline`, `text-start`/`text-end`) and RTL-compatible Tailwind utilities. Do not ship an English left/right layout and patch RTL afterward.
- **Radix UI and shadcn/ui** must behave correctly in RTL: menus, popovers, dialogs, directional icons, and keyboard interaction.
- **Mixed-direction content** (Persian + English, names, numbers, phone numbers, URLs, emails, medical abbreviations, code) must stay readable; isolate Latin spans with `dir="ltr"` / `lang="en"` or `<code>` where needed.
- User-facing labels, validation errors, empty states, confirmations, and toasts must be **natural Persian**. English UI text only when the user explicitly requests it.

## Typography and formatting

- Inspect existing fonts and assets before choosing typography. **No local font files** exist in the repo today; [src/app/layout.tsx](src/app/layout.tsx) uses Latin `next/font` subsets (Geist, Inter) — not a Persian type system.
- Do **not** download or install a font dependency without user approval; propose options after inspection.
- Ensure Persian and Latin text, punctuation, and numerals render without awkward spacing or clipping.
- **Currency:** Do not assume toman or rial. Ask the user before fixing the convention, or keep the display unit configurable. `Asia/Tehran` is not an implemented default timezone.
- Do **not** add a calendar library or general i18n framework without approval. If dates or numeric formatting are needed, inspect the project and propose an approach first.

## Design and verification

- Avoid literal translation of English-first layouts; use wording and alignment natural for Persian reading direction.
- Physician public sites are configured through validated settings. Customization must not break RTL, accessibility, or the design-system constraints in [ui-conventions.mdc](.cursor/rules/ui-conventions.mdc).
- Verify RTL layout at **mobile, tablet, and desktop** when implementing or reviewing UI (browser tools when available).
